# `T3`'s ACCEPTANCE — a walk that the WORLD can see, with no levelling anywhere.
#
# ⛔ WALK_TICK.md's step table gives `T3` the surprise *"`deck.keys` headless == the
# server's md5"*, and `deck.keys` CANNOT RUN AT `T3`: it says `send 6:1`, and making
# `6:` LEVEL a performed message is `T4`. Every walking fixture in `probe/t1/` levels,
# and probe 4 already recorded the reason — **a walk that does not level writes
# nothing**, so a saved world cannot see one.
#
# ⚠ SO THIS ASKS THE OTHER HALF OF WHAT A WALK DOES: IT POSITIONS. A `verb` is applied
# AT the author, and after 90 ticks the author is 9.6 wu from where a teleport left
# them — which is world-visible with no stamp of any kind. That is `K3e`'s own
# predicate, asked as a measurement instead of as a refusal.
#
# The pieces, and each is here for one reason:
#
#   verb raise   the ground is not flat, so the feet are a real height and the fall
#                has something to do. On flat ground `author_on` and `ground_under`
#                agree and the height change this step makes would be invisible.
#   step 90      the same walk `deck.keys` takes, so it sits on the plateau `T0`
#                measured (86, 88 -> one world; 90 … 98 -> another) rather than on
#                its cliff.
#   step 30      the walk is released and the fall settles, exactly as `deck.keys`
#                does before it builds.
#   verb place   a house, at wherever the walk ended. THIS is the assertion: 27 cells
#                and 84 wall edges land 9.6 wu away, or they land at the origin.
#
# ⚠ `30`, NOT `0`, AND THAT IS THE FIXTURE'S OWN FIRST FINDING. At yaw 0 the house is
# refused — *"a footprint at this facing has no mitred corners; turn one step"* — and a
# refusal writes nothing, so the run exits 0 with a world that cannot see the walk. The
# six mitre facings are what `tools/scripts/house.keys` says `30` for, and a fixture
# whose subject is a POSITION has to survive its own gesture before it can measure one.
rate 0
at 0 0 30
verb raise
wait rebuilt
keys 1
step 90
keys 0
step 30
feet
verb place
save t3walk
